    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1204">

                <pb facs="1101" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Ei9/63</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2708]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 16, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 29</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acquaint you that on
                    December 3 I received from His Majesty’s Foreign Office a note, a copy of which
                    I attach herewith,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1204-f1"/> requesting that inquiries be
                    made of the German Government concerning the identity of one Lieutenant zur See
                    Henry Koch, who recently escaped from internment at Norfolk. This inquiry was
                    accordingly transmitted to the Embassy at Berlin on December 7, with the request
                    that the desired particulars might be obtained.</p>
                <p>On December 6 Lieutenant Koch, who is now detained at Edinburgh, addressed a
                    communication to the Consul there who immediately transmitted it to this
                    Embassy. Copies of Koch’s letter and the Consul’s letter of transmittal were
                    presented to His Majesty’s Foreign Office on December 13, and I have the honor
                    to transmit herewith copies of these two communications.</p>
                <p>No reply has been made by this Embassy to the suggestion made in Lieutenant
                    Koch’s letter to the Consul at Edinburgh.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Hines Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d1204-a1.xml" xpointer="d1204-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d1204-a2.xml" xpointer="d1204-a2"/>
